From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:15:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: Disconnect requestCompleted when closing the
 camera

gst_libcamera_src_open() connects the camera's requestCompleted signal
to the element's state, and gst_libcamera_src_close() releases the
camera without disconnecting it. The Camera outlives the element, held
by the CameraManager, so:

- reopening the same element (NULL to READY again) connects a second
  slot, every request completes twice, and the second call pops another
  request: "assertion 'wrap->request_.get() == request' failed";
- a new element for the same camera leaves the old, freed state
  connected, and the next completed request crashes in
  GstLibcameraSrcState::requestCompleted().

Disconnect the state's slot before releasing the camera.

Tested on a Zinwa Q25 (MT6789, S5KJN1 and IMX111): a Qt Multimedia app
that stops and starts its camera, and one that recreates it, both kept
streaming where each crashed on the first restart.
---
 src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp b/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
index 9541aa3f..791099ec 100644
--- a/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
+++ b/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
@@ -974,6 +974,8 @@ gst_libcamera_src_close(GstLibcameraSrc *self)
 
 	state->config_.reset();
 
+	state->cam_->requestCompleted.disconnect(state);
+
 	ret = state->cam_->release();
 	if (ret) {
 		GST_ELEMENT_WARNING(self, RESOURCE, BUSY,
